A valkyrie routinely does the quest before the Castle; all you need for
the valkyrie quest is a decent weapon (like, say, Mjollnir or
Excalibur), decent HP (120 or so is good enough), and decent AC (-10 is
definitely good enough and I've done it with -6). The usual annoyance
value pertaining to fighting a covetous foe without yourself having
TP+TC applies, of course.

>Regardless, we're kind of splitting hairs; neither quest is very
>dangerous (unlike, say, the Samurai quest or the Monk quest).

The Samurai quest is mostly trivial as long as you have reflection
(there's a decent chance at least one of the ninja will have a wand of
death, and on my Samurai ascension I picked up /three/ charged wands of
death from the quest!); AT is nasty, but unlike MK or (I believe...) the
Chromatic Dragon he can be oneshotted with a death ray.

For the Caveman quest you have to prepare for random dragon breath and
be equipped to deal with invisible opponents who jig around you and can
cast Summon Nasties.
